// Pauli-X: the quantum NOT gate.
//
// Concept
//   X exchanges |0> and |1>. On a basis state it behaves exactly like a
//   classical bit flip, which makes it the right place to start: not everything
//   quantum is probabilistic.
//
// Expected quantum behaviour
//   The qubit ends in |1>, so measurement yields 1 every single time. There is
//   no randomness here at all.
//
// Expected measurement results
//   `result` is 1 in 100% of shots.
//
// Mathematical interpretation
//   X = [[0, 1], [1, 0]], so X|0> = |1>. The outcome probability is
//   |<1|X|0>|^2 = 1.
//
// @expect qubits=1 clbits=1 gates=1
// @expect-state |1>=1.0
// @expect-outcome 1

qubit q;
bit result;

x q;

measure q -> result;
